# Line endings, decided once.
#
# Without this, Git guesses per-machine: on Windows it rewrites LF to CRLF on
# checkout and back on commit, which produces "warning: LF will be replaced by
# CRLF" on every add and can show files as modified that nobody touched.
#
# LF in the repository for everything. Editors on Windows handle LF fine, and a
# repository whose contents depend on which machine cloned it is a repository
# that will one day produce a diff nobody wrote.
#
# NOT the same choice as the CRM repo, which is CRLF throughout because it grew
# that way and its guards assert it byte for byte. Two repos, two conventions,
# each internally consistent — which is the point of them being two repos.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
